                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7aeb4586-3021-3a79-8ee0-96ae62ce808d",
                                        "entry_id": "85b6c9f4-1141-3777-b0e2-628fb6af9658",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pour une application (ou une fonction) f:X↦Y et une partie B de l’ensemble d’arrivée Y : ensemble des éléments de l’ensemble de départ X dont l’image appartient à B : synonyme de préimage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7e7d289-5ab0-4088-b49c-e59e3fa7b0eb",
                                                "sense_id": "7aeb4586-3021-3a79-8ee0-96ae62ce808d",
                                                "text": "L’image réciproque de +4;+9 par f(x)=x² dans les nombres réels est -3;-2;+2;+3."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c405f01-0e05-4acc-9b95-86abeb1308d7",
                                                "sense_id": "7aeb4586-3021-3a79-8ee0-96ae62ce808d",
                                                "text": "L’image réciproque de -4 par f(x)=x² dans les nombres réels est l’ensemble vide ∅, car un carré est toujours nul ou positif."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fdbf756-aa18-4b1a-b5d7-887c003df15b",
                                                "sense_id": "7aeb4586-3021-3a79-8ee0-96ae62ce808d",
                                                "text": "L’image réciproque de -4 par f(x)=x² dans les nombres complexes est -2i;+2i."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "26c834ac-afee-47ac-928f-e7823781f486",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d5bdaef-e683-3875-ae25-f5c8126ddafa",
                        "source_sense_id": "3d9e0030-054b-38ed-a0b8-261865864afc",
                        "source_sense_description": "Element aus der Definitionsmenge, dem ein Element aus der Zielmenge zugeordnet wird",
                        "target_lang_word": "préimage",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "préimage",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1274287-41b3-330d-8424-f4f1d1a8ea72",
                                        "entry_id": "9917ab7e-0b7a-3734-a837-e6f99b3d3b88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pour une application f définie d’un ensemble X à un ensemble Y (f:X↦Y) et un sous-ensemble B de l’ensemble de destination Y (B⊆Y), la préimage de B, f⁻¹(B), est l’ensemble des éléments de X envoyés dans B par f :\\nf⁻¹(B)=x∈X∣f(x)∈B."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4cf9663a-10c2-3903-b358-27f64891a9be",
                                        "entry_id": "9917ab7e-0b7a-3734-a837-e6f99b3d3b88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pour un seul élément y de l’ensemble de destination, la préimage de y∈Y est définie par : f⁻¹(y)=x∈X∣f(x)=y, c’est-à-dire l’ensemble des antécédents de y."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7e69eb65-1203-4b51-b1e5-f882d8a9928b",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d5bdaef-e683-3875-ae25-f5c8126ddafa",
                        "source_sense_id": "4ba2cf58-fe04-3862-954e-292e68461e50",
                        "source_sense_description": "Teilmenge der Definitionsmenge, deren Elemente auf eine bestimmte Teilmenge der Zielmenge abgebildet werden",
                        "target_lang_word": "inverse image",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inverse image",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63a83409-53c0-3c07-9a73-03430969baa7",
                                        "entry_id": "aa2d304f-9633-34c5-a504-3f353fed72af",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of points that map to a given point (or set of points) under a specified function."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84e0390a-5a75-4bb7-9098-d9a1e15a7420",
                                                "sense_id": "63a83409-53c0-3c07-9a73-03430969baa7",
                                                "text": "Under the function given by f(x)#61;x², the inverse image of 4 is #92;#123;-2,2#92;#125;, as is the inverse image of #92;#123;4#92;#125;."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "85ad0343-cbad-40da-ab7f-9fb6d403eeee",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d5bdaef-e683-3875-ae25-f5c8126ddafa",
                        "source_sense_id": "4ba2cf58-fe04-3862-954e-292e68461e50",
                        "source_sense_description": "Teilmenge der Definitionsmenge, deren Elemente auf eine bestimmte Teilmenge der Zielmenge abgebildet werden",
                        "target_lang_word": "preimage",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "preimage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57f30964-aa7b-34fb-816b-a413f395b492",
                                        "entry_id": "b028ba15-d4ce-3b90-938b-60b7342d8bd7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For a given function, the set of all elements of the domain that are mapped into a given subset of the codomain; (formally) given a function ƒ : X → Y and a subset B ⊆ Y, the set ƒ⁻¹(B) = {x ∈ X : ƒ(x) ∈ B}."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "175d0626-bbcf-43d6-aff8-1c904b9d8ece",
                                                "sense_id": "57f30964-aa7b-34fb-816b-a413f395b492",
                                                "text": "The preimage of #92;#123;4,9#92;#125; under the function f#58;#92;R#92;rightarrow#92;R#58;f(x)#61;x² is the set #92;#123;-3,-2,#43;2,#43;3#92;#125;."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3de5b414-7e67-46a6-9a49-2564c94785a2",
                                                "sense_id": "57f30964-aa7b-34fb-816b-a413f395b492",
                                                "text": "1967 [Academic Press], Francois Treves, Topological Vector Spaces, Distributions and Kernels, 2006, Dover, page 22,\nThe preimage of a neighborhood U of 0 in E must be a neighborhood of (0,x), since (0,x) is mapped into 0."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e377505-a7ff-4872-8aae-b7c1cab1a9cf",
                                                "sense_id": "57f30964-aa7b-34fb-816b-a413f395b492",
                                                "text": "Previously, maps and hypermaps were constructed as the preimages of a segment joining two of the three critical values."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bdd390b-a282-4c3c-909e-0eeea446e91b",
                                                "sense_id": "57f30964-aa7b-34fb-816b-a413f395b492",
                                                "text": "Loosely speaking, saying that a function f is one-way implies that given y (in the range of f) it is infeasible to find a preimage of y under f."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
